window.docContents[105].resolve({"/UsingLean/#Logical-Foundations--UsingLean___-Using-the-full-power-of-a-proof-assistant--Using-the-Standard-Library":{"contents":"\n\nUse the exact? tactic to search for relevant theorems in the standard library.\n\nexample (a b : Nat) : a + b = b + a := by\n  /- this will suggest that we use `exact Nat.add_comm a b` to close this goal -/\n  exact?\n\n\n\n\nYou can also use rw? to look for theorems to rewrite by\n\nexample (a b : Nat) : a + b = b + a := by\n  /- this will suggest that we use `rw [Nat.add_comm]` to close this goal -/\n  rw?\n\n\n\n\nexample (n m q : Nat) :\n   (n + m) + q = m + (n + q) := by\n  -- lots of suggestions to look through here!\n  rw?\n  sorry\n\n\nProve the following theorems about Nats. You should not need induction for any of these;\nyou can find the theorems you need using rw? and exact?.\n\ntheorem mul_three (p : Nat) :\n    3 * p = p + p + p := by\n  sorry\n\n\n\n\ntheorem mul_three_beq (p : Nat) :\n    (3 * p == p + p + p) = true := by\n  sorry\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009UsingLean: Using the full power of a proof assistant","header":"4.2. Using the Standard Library","id":"/UsingLean/#Logical-Foundations--UsingLean___-Using-the-full-power-of-a-proof-assistant--Using-the-Standard-Library"}});